  "summary": "On Windows volumes with 8.3 short names, `actix_files::Files` can serve hidden",
  "details": "On Windows volumes with 8.3 short names, `actix_files::Files` can serve hidden\nfiles through their short-name aliases. The default path check rejects segments\nthat start with a dot, but an alias such as `ENV~1` or `GIT~1` passes this check.\n\nA remote client can read files such as `.env` or `.git/config` in the served\ndirectory even when `use_hidden_files()` is not enabled. This can expose secrets\nor source code.\n\nUpgrade to actix-files 0.7.4 or later. As a workaround, remove sensitive files\nand directories from the served directory.",
